<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10536" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιστράτηγος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ρᾰ]</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>enemy's general,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sert.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> at Rome,
				<i>acting commander</i> or <i>governor,</i> either <i>pro
				consule,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				28.3.1
			</span></i>, or <i>pro praetore,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				41.43
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>propraetor,</i> i.e. <i>governor</i> of a province with rank
			of <i>pro praetore,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12(5).722
			</span></i> (Andros, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>lieutenant</i> of a commander, Lat. <i>legatus pro
			praetore</i>, <u>OGI</u>ii<i><span class="en">
				p.551
			</span></i> (Bargylia, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.106.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Comp.Lys.Sull.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, etc.; in full, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρεσβευτὴς καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					14.12.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιταμίας καὶ ἀ.</span>
			proquaestor <i>pro praetore</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				448
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρεσβευτὴς Σεβαστοῦ
				ἀ.,</span>
			= Lat. <i>legatus Augusti pro praetore,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IGRom.
				3.186
			</span></i> (Ancyra, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), etc.</div>
